# Night Autonomous Coding Rule

- The local LLM is a bounded worker, not the orchestrator.
- Only explicit NIGHT_SAFE tasks may run unattended.
- Tool calls must be policy-validated.
- Never execute arbitrary model-emitted shell commands.
- No Git push or destructive Git.
- No secret/private-data access.
- No Discord sends, voice capture/training, CCTV configuration, or public deployment.
- Refuse unsafe/dirty workspace by default.
- Use bounded attempts/time/diff scope.
- Acceptance tests, not model confidence, determine PASS.
- Reset model context after each task and persist state to files.
- Cloud escalation is optional; quota failure must not stop independent local tasks.
- Windows scheduling is opt-in and must never be installed automatically.